      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ancramdale became the birthplace of northern bluegrass with the 1976 Berkshire Mountain Bluegrass Festival.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newpineplainsherald.org/ancramdale-the-cradle-of-northern-bluegrass/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nancy Talbott, a Cambridge music promoter, chose Ancramdale for its accessible location between NYC and Boston.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newpineplainsherald.org/ancramdale-the-cradle-of-northern-bluegrass/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Thirteen bands were hired for the inaugural festival, including five of the nation’s top bluegrass acts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newpineplainsherald.org/ancramdale-the-cradle-of-northern-bluegrass/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The festival site was a hillside field on the Rothvoss family farm, offering a natural amphitheater.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newpineplainsherald.org/ancramdale-the-cradle-of-northern-bluegrass/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "No incidents of rowdy behavior were reported, and police presence vanished after the second year.",
